worrying for the nation.


00:29:12.817 --> 00:29:14.842
Just worry about yourself.


00:29:14.919 --> 00:29:19.356
How could you tag along on
our wedding anniversary trip?


00:29:19.424 --> 00:29:22.860
Open the door! I have to pee!


00:29:22.927 --> 00:29:23.757
He's not answering.


00:29:23.828 --> 00:29:25.955
- He's not?
- No.


00:29:26.030 --> 00:29:28.555
I specifically told him
what time we'd be back.


00:29:28.633 --> 00:29:33.366
You had the keys when we left.


00:29:33.438 --> 00:29:34.063
I did?


00:29:34.139 --> 00:29:36.573
Just find it!


00:29:36.641 --> 00:29:37.869
Goddamn it.


00:29:37.942 --> 00:29:41.070
You're really in Mensa?


00:29:43.047 --> 00:29:45.174
<i>- I had the keys.
- Jeez, Mom!</i>


00:29:45.250 --> 00:29:46.979
Sheesh.


00:29:49.454 --> 00:29:51.888
Why is it so dark in here?


00:29:55.360 --> 00:29:56.486
Seok-woo.


00:29:58.663 --> 00:29:59.789
Are you all right?


00:30:03.067 --> 00:30:04.796
He didn't clean up all week.


00:30:04.869 --> 00:30:06.200
What a mess.


00:30:06.271 --> 00:30:08.501
Why, that little...


00:30:09.073 --> 00:30:12.008
Just look at that idiot
putting on an act.


00:30:13.278 --> 00:30:17.408
I wondered if he could handle
himself, but apparently not


00:30:17.982 --> 00:30:20.610
Look at him
just staring at us.


00:30:21.085 --> 00:30:22.313
What's that smell?


00:30:23.588 --> 00:30:25.112
He probably played
games all night.


00:30:25.190 --> 00:30:26.418
My liquor!


00:30:27.392 --> 00:30:29.724
I warned him
not to touch it...


00:30:31.296 --> 00:30:32.729
Seok-woo!


00:30:34.299 --> 00:30:35.630
What's wrong with you?


00:30:38.603 --> 00:30:40.730
- What's wrong with him?
- Seok-woo!


00:30:42.807 --> 00:30:44.832
Son!
What's gotten into you?


00:30:50.114 --> 00:30:53.743
Seok-woo! It's Dad!


00:31:03.862 --> 00:31:08.993
He has to try on
the pants I bought him...


00:31:10.268 --> 00:31:14.602
Seok-woo, Mommy...


00:31:14.672 --> 00:31:18.005
My 30-year-old Ballantine's...


00:31:20.578 --> 00:31:22.409
Johnnie walker Blue Label...


00:31:24.582 --> 00:31:28.313
Jack Daniel's Single Barrel...


00:31:59.450 --> 00:32:01.577
I told them
we shouldn't come back.


00:32:33.084 --> 00:32:37.020
<i>We've received reports that
the virus symptoms have mutated.</i>


00:32:37.088 --> 00:32:39.818
<i>Uncontrollable libido
appetite, and depression...</i>


00:32:39.891 --> 00:32:41.518
<i>Patients had been
suffering from</i>


00:32:41.592 --> 00:32:43.423
<i>symptoms related
to such human vices.</i>


00:32:43.494 --> 00:32:46.327
<i>Now they've lost
all cognitive abilities</i>


00:32:46.397 --> 00:32:49.423
<i>and are attacking
others at random.</i>


00:32:49.500 --> 00:32:51.832
<i>The number of casualties
is skyrocketing.</i>


00:32:57.008 --> 00:32:58.737
<i>They may appear to be
living human beings,</i>


00:32:58.810 --> 00:33:01.370
<i>but experts call them</i>


00:33:01.446 --> 00:33:03.573
<i>"dead bodies
in suspended animation".</i>


00:33:03.648 --> 00:33:05.479
<i>Please refrain
from going outdoors</i>


00:33:05.550 --> 00:33:07.575
<i>and stay somewhere safe.</i>


00:33:12.557 --> 00:33:15.788
<i>If you see any people moaning
or walking very slowly,</i>


00:33:15.860 --> 00:33:18.385
<i>we advise you
to flee immediately</i>


00:33:18.463 --> 00:33:20.590
<i>or to report
to the nearest police.</i>


00:33:20.665 --> 00:33:22.292
<i>An unverified report
states that</i>


00:33:22.367 --> 00:33:24.494
<i>even deaths have occurred.</i>


00:33:28.873 --> 00:33:30.500
<i>Unbelievable breaking news.</i>


00:33:30.575 --> 00:33:32.008
<i>Victims believed
to have been murdered</i>


00:33:32.076 --> 00:33:35.011
<i>by the virus patients</i>


00:33:35.079 --> 00:33:38.207
<i>have been coming back to life
in immediate suspended animation.</i>


00:33:38.282 --> 00:33:43.015
<i>Symptoms of the unidentified
virus have quickly mutated.</i>


00:33:44.789 --> 00:33:50.022
<i>Experts are working nonstop to
find the cause of this phenomenon,</i>


00:33:50.161 --> 00:33:56.794
<i>but even cutting edge science
cannot explain these events.</i>


00:34:02.140 --> 00:34:06.270
<i>A reporter from Seoul Monthly
released a controversial theory online,</i>


00:34:06.344 --> 00:34:11.145
<i>claiming this epidemic to be
of North Korea's doing,</i>


00:34:11.282 --> 00:34:15.241
<i>and that talk of withdrawal of
U.S. Forces was the cause.</i>


00:34:17.855 --> 00:34:20.790
<i>A far-right politician
claims this to be</i>


00:34:20.858 --> 00:34:23.292
<i>nationalists' vendetta
against himself.</i>


00:34:23.361 --> 00:34:25.488
<i>He has applied
for asylum in Japan,</i>


00:34:25.563 --> 00:34:27.497
<i>but it was denied again.</i>


00:35:31.863 --> 00:35:34.991
<i>Some have also
suggested reinstating</i>


00:35:35.066 --> 00:35:39.093
<i>of Dr. HWANG to study
the virus.</i>


00:35:39.170 --> 00:35:41.900
<i>Members of HWANG's advocate
group, "HWANG Forever",</i>


00:35:41.973 --> 00:35:43.998
<i>visited
the Ministry of Environment</i>


00:35:44.075 --> 00:35:46.100
<i>to request a meeting
with the Minister.</i>


00:35:47.578 --> 00:35:49.409
<i>Most online comments on handling</i>


00:35:49.480 --> 00:35:52.608
<i>virus patient attacks
were proven false.</i>


00:35:52.683 --> 00:35:54.514
<i>As analysts believe this is</i>


00:35:54.585 --> 00:35:56.109
<i>another instance
of cyber-bullying,</i>


00:35:56.187 --> 00:35:58.712
<i>some claim protesters of the</i>


00:35:58.789 --> 00:36:01.849
<i>online real-name system
are responsible.</i>


00:36:02.326 --> 00:36:04.260
<i>The American Secretary of Defense</i>


00:36:04.328 --> 00:36:05.761
<i>has reported
to the U.S. President</i>


00:36:05.830 --> 00:36:06.956
<i>that "such biochemical attacks
must not be ignored",</i>


00:36:07.031 --> 00:36:09.261
<i>and that "drastic measures</i>


00:36:09.333 --> 00:36:12.461
<i>must be considered
to ensure world peace".</i>


00:37:39.156 --> 00:37:43.593
<i>Do you think we'll
remember this moment?</i>


00:38:19.530 --> 00:38:21.862
<i>And the LORD God commanded
the man, saying,</i>


00:38:21.932 --> 00:38:24.059
<i>"Of every tree of
the garden you may freely eat;</i>


00:38:24.135 --> 00:38:26.569
<i>but of the tree of
the knowledge of good and evil</i>


00:38:26.637 --> 00:38:28.070
<i>you shall not eat
for in the day that you eat of it</i>


00:38:28.139 --> 00:38:30.073
<i>you shall surely die."
Genesis 2: 16-17</i>


00:39:18.723 --> 00:39:21.954
Robot assistance
fortunately allows us


00:39:22.026 --> 00:39:24.051
to focus on our practices.


00:39:24.729 --> 00:39:26.253
Do they take care of cleaning?


00:39:26.330 --> 00:39:29.458
No, our monks do the cleaning.


00:39:30.134 --> 00:39:32.159
Cleaning is part
of our practices,


00:39:32.236 --> 00:39:35.672
but money management is not.


00:39:35.740 --> 00:39:40.074
<i>What kind of duties does the
defective RU-4 have here?</i>


00:39:40.144 --> 00:39:45.582
In-myung is a guide robot who
provides general information.


00:39:45.649 --> 00:39:50.086
But calling him "defective"
does not seem suitable.


00:39:50.154 --> 00:39:52.088
If he's not defective...


00:39:52.156 --> 00:39:54.681
Are you saying
he thinks on his own,


00:39:54.759 --> 00:39:57.887
rather than repeating
the input data?


00:39:57.962 --> 00:40:00.590
Correct. He shares
his own realizations


00:40:00.664 --> 00:40:04.896
with our believers
and other monks.


00:40:04.969 --> 00:40:07.904
But don't monks struggle
to attain enlightenment?


00:40:07.972 --> 00:40:10.202
You're saying a robot
has attained it?


00:40:11.575 --> 00:40:16.205
Howbeit, we have heard
his teachings,


00:40:16.280 --> 00:40:19.511
and have acknowledged
his spiritual growth.


00:40:20.184 --> 00:40:24.120
Instead of repairing or checking
for In-myung's defects,


00:40:24.188 --> 00:40:31.526
we seek your professional
judgment on his current state.


00:40:36.300 --> 00:40:38.928
There is In-myung.


00:41:49.006 --> 00:41:50.439
Turn your head.


00:42:18.769 --> 00:42:20.293
What? Are you curious?


00:42:20.771 --> 00:42:23.205
Please see me for what I am.


00:42:40.691 --> 00:42:42.420
Everything looks normal.


00:42:43.193 --> 00:42:45.320
I am normal.


00:42:45.996 --> 00:42:48.021
I wasn't talking to you, robot.


00:42:49.199 --> 00:42:52.032
<i>I realize this must be
stressful for you.</i>


00:42:53.304 --> 00:42:54.635
What are you talking about?


00:42:54.705 --> 00:42:58.436
It is all right.
I am just a machine.


00:42:58.509 --> 00:43:00.568
Please feel at ease.


00:43:00.644 --> 00:43:02.271
I am.


00:43:03.547 --> 00:43:06.482
I've handled hundreds of
troublesome robots like you.


00:43:08.752 --> 00:43:11.084
I do not understand
why UR International


00:43:11.155 --> 00:43:15.091
sent a repair specialist.


00:43:15.159 --> 00:43:16.990
I'm here at
the temple's request.


00:43:18.462 --> 00:43:21.590
I know we did not request
a repair specialist.


00:43:23.867 --> 00:43:27.394
A specialist
first checks in-person


00:43:27.471 --> 00:43:29.905
for defects or need of service.


00:43:31.075 --> 00:43:32.201
It's protocol.


00:43:34.178 --> 00:43:35.907
Then you have confirmed


00:43:35.980 --> 00:43:39.507
that I have no defects.


00:43:39.583 --> 00:43:41.107
That's not for you to decide.


00:43:41.185 --> 00:43:43.312
All is functional
is it not?


00:43:54.598 --> 00:43:56.725
This matter is beyond
my authority.


00:43:58.202 --> 00:44:00.466
I do not understand.


00:44:00.537 --> 00:44:03.370
I don't know what
you're asking of me.


00:44:04.341 --> 00:44:06.275
I know nothing about Buddhism.


00:44:07.044 --> 00:44:08.568
If a robot is defective,


00:44:08.646 --> 00:44:12.275
I change its parts
and repair it.


00:44:12.349 --> 00:44:15.079
If it's worse
I report to the head office.


00:44:15.152 --> 00:44:17.382
My job is to fix
defective robots.


00:44:18.555 --> 00:44:20.386
But you're telling me
this robot is Buddha.


00:44:21.058 --> 00:44:23.686
<i>If this crazy robot claims
he's Buddha,</i>


00:44:23.761 --> 00:44:27.595
it's my job to open him up
and repair the short circuit.


00:44:27.665 --> 00:44:30.600
But you want me to confirm
if he is Buddha.


00:44:30.668 --> 00:44:31.999
You are not at fault, sir.


00:44:32.069 --> 00:44:34.299
Stay out of this!
Humans are talking!


00:44:46.784 --> 00:44:50.117
<i>I apologize
if we have offended you.</i>


00:44:51.088 --> 00:44:54.717
I had thought seeing him
for yourself would be best.


00:44:54.792 --> 00:44:59.456
I'm afraid
my actions were rash.


00:45:00.030 --> 00:45:02.464
This is beyond my authority.


00:45:02.533 --> 00:45:05.161
I'll file a recall
according to protocol.


00:45:06.036 --> 00:45:09.164
In-myung is no mere robot.


00:45:13.243 --> 00:45:14.676
That's for us to decide.


00:45:14.745 --> 00:45:18.977
Yes, it is a matter for you
experts to decide.


00:45:19.049 --> 00:45:21.882
So what have you decided?


00:45:21.952 --> 00:45:24.284
Even if In-myung is not Buddha,


00:45:24.354 --> 00:45:28.381
don't you agree that he is
different from other robots?


00:45:28.459 --> 00:45:31.895
It's just a robot
like I'm just a technician.


00:45:31.962 --> 00:45:34.692
Why do you experts
only believe data?


00:45:34.765 --> 00:45:37.495
Why won't you allow
room for imagination?


00:45:37.568 --> 00:45:40.696
Why must data be truth
and all else be false?


00:45:40.771 --> 00:45:42.602
What are you saying?


00:45:42.673 --> 00:45:47.201
Then would you have me explore
philosophy with the robot?


00:45:47.277 --> 00:45:50.906
I am asking you to
look again without fear.


00:45:52.082 --> 00:45:53.208
Fine.


00:45:53.283 --> 00:45:54.910
If you cannot determine whether


00:45:54.985 --> 00:45:57.112
In-myung is Buddha or not,


00:45:57.187 --> 00:46:00.748
then can you not at least see
the hearts of people?


00:46:00.824 --> 00:46:03.850
The reason for our actions...


00:46:03.927 --> 00:46:05.758
The reason for our bringing
a busy technician here.


00:46:05.829 --> 00:46:09.060
Can you not see it?


00:46:10.334 --> 00:46:13.770
Please check Brother
In-myung once more.


00:46:17.241 --> 00:46:20.677
All I see
is a defective robot.


00:46:26.350 --> 00:46:27.874
I will go now.


00:47:02.019 --> 00:47:05.853
- Who is it?
- Hey...


00:47:06.123 --> 00:47:09.650
Is the repair guy here?


00:47:18.235 --> 00:47:19.668
What guy?


00:47:19.736 --> 00:47:23.672
Hi. You're the guy
who fixes robots, right?


00:47:27.845 --> 00:47:29.972
Yes. So?


00:47:30.047 --> 00:47:33.073
Fix my baby for me.


00:47:35.752 --> 00:47:39.586
- What is this?
- My baby.


00:47:42.759 --> 00:47:45.785
I think she's dead.
She won't move.


00:47:45.863 --> 00:47:48.297
So just lend me a chip.


00:47:48.365 --> 00:47:51.198
You fix robots.
I'm sure you have a lot.


00:47:51.268 --> 00:47:54.601
No, you need to take this
to a robot pet center.


00:47:54.671 --> 00:47:56.195
But she died all of a sudden


00:47:56.273 --> 00:47:58.400
and the center is closed now.


00:47:58.475 --> 00:48:02.434
I've been waiting for you
to come home for hours.


00:48:02.512 --> 00:48:04.742
I was waiting for you
and it's too late now!


00:48:05.415 --> 00:48:07.849
So just give me one chip.


00:48:07.918 --> 00:48:11.354
Just wait until tomorrow and
go to the center when it opens.


00:48:12.322 --> 00:48:14.552
But I need her right now!


00:49:00.704 --> 00:49:02.638
Don't you know that
smoking is illegal?


00:49:05.909 --> 00:49:07.342
Did you fix her?


00:49:08.211 --> 00:49:10.645
It's temporary.
I don't have the right chip.


00:49:11.214 --> 00:49:13.444
It'll be fine to play with
for a few hours.


00:49:17.321 --> 00:49:20.347
Damn it. It moves awkward.


00:49:24.428 --> 00:49:25.759
You really don't have it?


00:49:29.733 --> 00:49:31.564
Go to this place tomorrow.


00:49:31.635 --> 00:49:34.263
They carry the best biochips
in the country.


00:49:40.844 --> 00:49:44.371
I'm not quite happy with it
but thanks anyway.


00:49:47.250 --> 00:49:50.481
So do you live
with robots too?


00:49:50.554 --> 00:49:51.885
Excuse me?


00:49:51.955 --> 00:49:54.287
Do you live alone
with robots?


00:49:54.358 --> 00:49:58.886
I see. No wonder.


00:50:00.263 --> 00:50:01.890
Let's go, baby.


00:50:30.594 --> 00:50:32.425
<i>More and more young people</i>


00:50:32.496 --> 00:50:35.624
<i>are choosing robots
over marriage.</i>


00:50:35.699 --> 00:50:38.532
<i>These so-called
"humanoid mates".</i>


00:50:38.602 --> 00:50:41.628
<i>With national birth rates
at record lows,</i>


00:50:41.705 --> 00:50:46.039
<i>such social trends are
a rising problem.</i>


00:50:47.010 --> 00:50:48.944
<i>They're actually
more trustworthy.</i>


00:50:49.012 --> 00:50:51.640
<i>We're practically family now.</i>


00:50:53.316 --> 00:50:54.943
Yes, ma'am.


00:50:55.018 --> 00:50:57.851
<i>Why don't I have your report?</i>


00:50:57.921 --> 00:50:59.286
Yes, I'll file it soon.


00:51:01.058 --> 00:51:03.083
<i>Is there a problem?</i>


00:51:03.160 --> 00:51:07.893
<i>I need your report to decide
what to do with the robot.</i>


00:51:08.065 --> 00:51:12.502
To be honest, I haven't
reached a decision yet.


00:51:12.569 --> 00:51:17.404
<i>What decision?
Is the robot still useful?</i>


00:51:20.177 --> 00:51:24.807
That's what
I cann't decide on.


00:51:24.881 --> 00:51:27.406
<i>Is it necessary to
exterminate RU-4?</i>


00:51:27.484 --> 00:51:31.921
<i>What? Look, Mr. PARK...</i>


00:51:31.988 --> 00:51:33.615
I'll file my report soon.


00:52:27.177 --> 00:52:29.202
Would you like to come in?


00:52:38.989 --> 00:52:41.014
What brings you here
at this hour?


00:52:41.992 --> 00:52:46.520
I've come for advice
for my troubled mind.


00:52:46.596 --> 00:52:48.223
What troubles you?


00:52:48.798 --> 00:52:51.232
I was quite upset
by the encounter


00:52:51.301 --> 00:52:53.428
with the technician
this afternoon.


00:52:53.503 --> 00:52:56.438
Why did it upset you?


00:52:56.506 --> 00:52:58.235
I learned that
all awakened beings


00:52:58.308 --> 00:53:00.572
in this world are Buddha,


00:53:01.344 --> 00:53:05.576
and you have attained
the highest point among us all.


00:53:05.649 --> 00:53:09.779
But they deem you defective
and order a recall.


00:53:09.853 --> 00:53:12.981
He merely did
what he had to do.


00:53:13.056 --> 00:53:14.489
That is not all.


00:53:14.958 --> 00:53:18.792
The company will send a team of
exterminators tomorrow.


00:53:19.663 --> 00:53:21.995
It is absolutely absurd.


00:53:22.065 --> 00:53:24.795
As if you were some killer robot.


00:53:25.869 --> 00:53:29.100
I question their ability
of perception.


00:53:30.974 --> 00:53:34.000
You will be in great danger
if we do nothing.


00:53:44.087 --> 00:53:47.318
What do you see me as?


00:53:48.391 --> 00:53:49.915
You are Buddha.


00:53:50.594 --> 00:53:53.028
What does that appear to be?


00:53:56.700 --> 00:53:59.168
That is a clock.


00:54:14.451 --> 00:54:16.783
Then what does
this appear to be?


00:54:18.154 --> 00:54:21.385
Is this my arm
or is it a clock?


00:54:25.962 --> 00:54:28.692
To perceive is to distinguish,


00:54:28.765 --> 00:54:32.997
merely a classification
of knowing.


00:54:33.069 --> 00:54:37.005
While all living creatures share
the same inherent nature,


00:54:37.073 --> 00:54:39.598
perception is
what classifies one


00:54:39.676 --> 00:54:42.907
as Buddha and
another as machine.


00:54:42.979 --> 00:54:47.712
We mistake perception
as permanent truth


00:54:47.784 --> 00:54:50.514
and such delusions
cause us pain.


00:54:50.987 --> 00:54:55.822
Perception itself is void
as is the process of perceiving.


00:54:57.193 --> 00:55:00.754
As I am a perception
of this void,


00:55:00.830 --> 00:55:03.355
please see me for what I am.


00:55:05.035 --> 00:55:06.468
Brother In-myung.


00:55:13.243 --> 00:55:15.177
Fill your mind
with nothingness.


00:57:02.118 --> 00:57:07.647
From where have I come
and to where do I go?


00:57:09.125 --> 00:57:12.754
From where have I come,


00:57:12.829 --> 00:57:14.763
and to where do I go?


00:57:19.736 --> 00:57:22.068
What am I?


00:57:22.639 --> 00:57:24.470
What am I?


00:57:26.042 --> 00:57:28.374
What am I?


00:57:28.445 --> 00:57:32.279
From where have I come
and to where do I go?


00:57:34.350 --> 00:57:38.377
What am I?


00:57:39.856 --> 00:57:41.687
What am I?


00:57:43.359 --> 00:57:47.887
From where have I come
and to where do I go?


00:58:22.432 --> 00:58:24.161
When is this model from?


00:58:25.835 --> 00:58:28.770
The R200 series, circa 2017.


00:58:28.838 --> 00:58:30.362
Why was it not replaced?


00:58:30.440 --> 00:58:32.772
I'm sorry, sir.
We'll replace it now.


00:58:33.543 --> 00:58:34.669
Extermination team.


00:58:37.747 --> 00:58:40.181
That is not necessary.


00:58:40.250 --> 00:58:44.687
This robot is still useful
to our temple.


00:58:44.754 --> 00:58:46.984
We have the right
and responsibility to


00:58:47.056 --> 00:58:49.581
replace outdated models, sir.


00:58:49.659 --> 00:58:54.392
But if the buyer is satisfied
there is no need.


00:58:54.464 --> 00:58:56.989
I am still useful.


00:58:58.568 --> 00:59:02.231
I will begin my introduction
of our temple.


00:59:02.305 --> 00:59:03.237
- Mr. PARK.
- Yes, ma'am.


00:59:03.306 --> 00:59:06.139
- Did you check this?
- I checked it yesterday.


00:59:06.209 --> 00:59:08.234
I decided it
was still functional,


00:59:08.311 --> 00:59:09.744
so I did not report it.


00:59:09.812 --> 00:59:12.747
Report everything
and I'll decide.


00:59:12.815 --> 00:59:14.442
Yes, ma'am.


00:59:14.517 --> 00:59:15.950
You may go.


00:59:41.044 --> 00:59:44.275
I flew over as soon as I got
the emergency report.


00:59:44.347 --> 00:59:50.183
For failing to distinguish
such crucial matters as this,


00:59:50.253 --> 00:59:52.983
I fired nine secretaries and
one ignorant manager.


00:59:53.756 --> 00:59:56.190
Our technician seems to
grasp the situation.


00:59:57.260 --> 01:00:03.199
So why did you seek the guarantee
of UR from a mere technician,


01:00:03.766 --> 01:00:06.701
in trying to turn that robot
into Buddha?


01:00:07.870 --> 01:00:11.101
<i>I realize
that we were at fault.</i>


01:00:13.276 --> 01:00:15.005
You are not obligated to mind


01:00:15.078 --> 01:00:17.410
the interests
of a mere corporation.


01:00:17.480 --> 01:00:19.812
But UR is
essentially different


01:00:19.882 --> 01:00:22.009
from these companies
you think of.


01:00:22.785 --> 01:00:26.414
UR robots are in our governments
schools, and families.


01:00:26.489 --> 01:00:29.617
Simply put, they are integral
to all areas of society.


01:00:29.692 --> 01:00:32.820
You could say that UR provides


01:00:32.895 --> 01:00:34.726
the basic groundwork
of the human race.


01:00:34.797 --> 01:00:37.129
Must mankind
then refrain from


01:00:37.200 --> 01:00:39.430
breaking down its own foothold?


01:00:41.104 --> 01:00:42.628
I am stating that
one robot's defects


01:00:42.705 --> 01:00:46.232
can prove fatal
to the national system.


01:00:46.309 --> 01:00:49.745
Thus it is a threat of
the world of suffering.


01:00:49.812 --> 01:00:53.441
What did you say?
This is not a "threat".


01:00:53.516 --> 01:00:56.144
National security
is always an excuse


01:00:56.219 --> 01:00:58.050
used to suppress the people.


01:00:58.121 --> 01:01:00.885
Now used
by a mere corporation.


01:01:00.957 --> 01:01:02.288
Refrain yourself.


01:01:02.358 --> 01:01:04.087
No, that is not so.


01:01:05.261 --> 01:01:09.595
We're only discussing the
threat to mankind's existence.


01:01:09.666 --> 01:01:14.103
Whether UR is the cause or
the basis is not important.


01:01:14.170 --> 01:01:17.697
You only see a merchant in me,


01:01:17.774 --> 01:01:22.108
but keep this in mind.
UR's client is all of mankind.


01:01:23.079 --> 01:01:25.707
I can take measures
alike to heads of state


01:01:25.782 --> 01:01:29.513
against such threats to mankind.


01:01:30.887 --> 01:01:35.119
People often see science as
a mere instrument to mankind.


01:01:35.191 --> 01:01:37.022
A subservient
aid to do its bidding,


01:01:37.093 --> 01:01:39.527
like some genie in a lamp.


01:01:39.595 --> 01:01:43.622
But each scientific
advancement man utilizes


01:01:43.700 --> 01:01:47.636
is conversely
changing man himself.


01:01:47.704 --> 01:01:49.831
<i>Even before we realize it.</i>


01:01:49.906 --> 01:01:53.034
When the first man wielded
that wooden stick,


01:01:53.109 --> 01:01:57.239
the stick was also wielding him.


01:01:59.115 --> 01:02:03.882
Which is why we are training
ourselves to reach a balance


01:02:03.953 --> 01:02:06.478
between mind and matter.


01:02:08.958 --> 01:02:11.392
Quite optimistic.


01:02:11.461 --> 01:02:12.689
Man has been a slave
to material things


01:02:12.762 --> 01:02:16.789
since the dawn of civilization.


01:02:16.866 --> 01:02:18.891
Man has always
been marginalized


01:02:18.968 --> 01:02:20.993
by class, capital
and labor.


01:02:21.070 --> 01:02:23.095
And now we will be marginalized


01:02:23.172 --> 01:02:24.196
by a monster we created.


01:02:24.273 --> 01:02:26.798
Creator, at the will
of his own creation!


01:02:26.876 --> 01:02:28.207
Understand?


01:02:28.277 --> 01:02:30.404
All creators face the dilemma


01:02:30.480 --> 01:02:34.007
that they've created a monster.


01:02:34.083 --> 01:02:37.314
But every problem
has a solution.


01:02:37.386 --> 01:02:41.322
The solution is
to dismantle the RU.


01:02:41.390 --> 01:02:43.415
We see the problems of RU


01:02:43.493 --> 01:02:47.623
and the solution is
to obliterate these monsters.


01:02:47.697 --> 01:02:50.222
We must not let
its sly tongue fool us.


01:02:50.299 --> 01:02:51.926
We will be left at their mercy


01:02:52.001 --> 01:02:54.231
before we even know it.


01:02:55.905 --> 01:02:57.634
A different example.


01:02:57.707 --> 01:02:59.572
The human brain has not evolved


01:02:59.642 --> 01:03:01.667
since the dissemination
of computers,


01:03:01.744 --> 01:03:05.475
left only with basic
arithmetic functions.


01:03:10.553 --> 01:03:12.987
What is the main number
for this temple?


01:03:40.983 --> 01:03:42.211
Man has forever struggled


01:03:42.285 --> 01:03:45.015
to define its existence,


01:03:45.087 --> 01:03:48.113
but with no
satisfactory explanation.


01:03:48.191 --> 01:03:49.715
There was no necessity,


01:03:49.792 --> 01:03:52.022
for man was a singular being.


01:03:52.094 --> 01:03:54.119
But things have changed.


01:03:54.197 --> 01:03:56.927
Man is desperately trying to
define its existence,


01:03:56.999 --> 01:04:00.662
because a nearly
indistinguishable


01:04:00.736 --> 01:04:02.260
entity has emerged.


01:04:03.239 --> 01:04:05.867
That is this very entity!


01:04:08.044 --> 01:04:10.672
<i>Step forward, RU-4.</i>


01:04:21.757 --> 01:04:24.282
<i>RU-4, step forward!</i>


01:05:38.267 --> 01:05:40.701
The RU series is a failure.


01:05:41.671 --> 01:05:44.196
We have decided to exterminate


01:05:44.273 --> 01:05:46.605
all RU models around the world.


01:05:47.877 --> 01:05:49.708
RU was made by man,


01:05:49.779 --> 01:05:52.509
but it is now a threat to us.


01:05:52.581 --> 01:05:54.105
A threat that talks, thinks,


01:05:54.183 --> 01:05:56.515
cries,
and even laughs like man!


01:05:56.585 --> 01:05:58.917
Even invading religion and art!


01:05:58.988 --> 01:06:01.149
Get a hold of yourselves!


01:06:01.223 --> 01:06:06.251
That thing is a dagger held to
the very throat of mankind!


01:06:13.536 --> 01:06:15.060
I'm shocked to find that


01:06:15.137 --> 01:06:18.368
the president
of UR detests robots.


01:06:24.547 --> 01:06:28.381
If you still see me as just
a grumbling businessman,


01:06:29.251 --> 01:06:30.878
So be it.


01:06:31.554 --> 01:06:34.682
- Director MIN, get it ready.
- Yes, sir.


01:06:54.276 --> 01:06:56.710
<i>Greetings.</i>


01:06:56.779 --> 01:06:58.610
<i>Today's unexpected news from</i>


01:06:58.681 --> 01:07:01.844
<i>this unexpected source
was surprising.</i>


01:07:01.917 --> 01:07:04.647
<i>I am putting no one at fault.</i>


01:07:04.720 --> 01:07:09.851
<i>Each temple has authority to
reach its own decisions.</i>


01:07:09.925 --> 01:07:11.950
<i>But my brothers,</i>


01:07:12.028 --> 01:07:15.964
<i>ponder the effects
of a robot's awakening on us.</i>


01:07:16.432 --> 01:07:19.663
<i>What meaning can it hold for
our brothers elsewhere?</i>


01:07:19.735 --> 01:07:23.762
<i>What robot is desirous
or compulsive by nature?</i>


01:07:23.839 --> 01:07:25.864
<i>Are not robots created
without such desires,</i>


01:07:25.941 --> 01:07:31.277
<i>for the sole purpose
of serving man?</i>


01:07:31.347 --> 01:07:34.475
<i>If we were to acknowledge
a robot as Buddha...</i>


01:07:34.550 --> 01:07:37.075
<i>If it were constructed
inherent with enlightenment,</i>


01:07:37.153 --> 01:07:40.782
<i>which so few attain after
such struggle and denial of self,</i>


01:07:40.856 --> 01:07:45.384
<i>who would bear the countless</i>


01:07:45.461 --> 01:07:48.988
<i>cycles of death and
birth to achieve it?</i>


01:07:49.065 --> 01:07:51.295
<i>Answer me this, robot.</i>


01:07:51.367 --> 01:07:56.600
<i>Have you come to drive man away
from the path of awakening?</i>


01:07:56.672 --> 01:08:00.438
<i>You must know the effects of</i>


01:08:00.509 --> 01:08:02.739
<i>your talk of Nirvana
on these poor souls!</i>


01:08:04.513 --> 01:08:07.539
<i>If you have truly
been enlightened,</i>


01:08:07.616 --> 01:08:10.744
<i>attest to this by
withdrawing yourself now.</i>


01:08:12.521 --> 01:08:14.148
<i>Put an end to this, robot!</i>


01:08:18.227 --> 01:08:21.060
Everything has been revealed.


01:08:21.931 --> 01:08:25.560
This robot failed to answer
the Master monk's question.


01:08:25.634 --> 01:08:29.661
It is now clear that
this robot is defective.


01:08:29.738 --> 01:08:32.571
You will stand
witness to the end of


01:08:32.641 --> 01:08:34.973
a robot resisting human orders.


01:08:36.345 --> 01:08:39.075
- Carry out the order.
- Wait, sir.


01:08:39.148 --> 01:08:40.274
Just one minute.


01:08:41.951 --> 01:08:45.182
Please allow me some
more time, sir.


01:08:45.254 --> 01:08:49.190
Allow me some time to
run a check in more detail.


01:08:49.258 --> 01:08:50.589
What are you saying?


01:08:50.659 --> 01:08:52.388
<i>You once stated
that the RU-4 was</i>


01:08:52.461 --> 01:08:55.487
a turning point
in the history of man.


01:08:55.564 --> 01:08:58.192
Who could've known
its greatest gift


01:08:58.267 --> 01:09:00.531
would become
its mortal affliction?


01:09:00.603 --> 01:09:03.231
Technical error must be dealt
through technical means.


01:09:03.305 --> 01:09:06.331
Stop this, Mr. PARK.


01:09:06.408 --> 01:09:10.344
No, I have something to say.


01:09:10.412 --> 01:09:11.845
Sir, no one here is perfect,


01:09:11.914 --> 01:09:14.747
including you and I.


01:09:14.817 --> 01:09:18.548
But we are not exterminated
at the touch of a button.


01:09:18.621 --> 01:09:21.556
- We don't have time for this.
- Sir!


01:09:21.624 --> 01:09:23.558
A robot must not think.


01:09:23.626 --> 01:09:25.958
A robot must not
possess cognition.


01:09:26.028 --> 01:09:28.553
It must not have emotions
or feel pain.


01:09:28.631 --> 01:09:31.657
A robot must never construe or


01:09:31.734 --> 01:09:32.666
trespass on the domains of man!


01:09:32.735 --> 01:09:36.364
A robot must unconditionally
obey human orders!


01:09:36.438 --> 01:09:38.167
Begin immediately!


01:09:45.247 --> 01:09:48.774
<i>RU- 400745479 ExQ.</i>


01:09:48.851 --> 01:09:51.786
You are hereby subject to
Code Alpha 42 Plus.


01:09:52.655 --> 01:09:56.284
You must obey all further orders
and will now be collected.


01:09:56.759 --> 01:09:58.590
What say you, robot?


01:09:58.661 --> 01:10:01.596
You claim to
have reached Nirvana.


01:10:01.664 --> 01:10:05.191
Will you not obey
to the likes of man?


01:10:05.267 --> 01:10:06.291
Be warned!


01:10:06.368 --> 01:10:07.801
We are free
from legal constraints


01:10:07.870 --> 01:10:09.895
on robots violating this code,


01:10:09.972 --> 01:10:14.807
and will commence fire to
exterminate all such robots!


01:10:15.477 --> 01:10:16.910
Will you obey?


01:10:17.780 --> 01:10:19.509
Obey our orders.


01:10:22.585 --> 01:10:24.018
Obey our orders!


01:10:24.086 --> 01:10:27.419
This is your last warning!
Will you obey?


01:10:30.092 --> 01:10:33.027
As head of UR
I order to open fire!


01:10:37.499 --> 01:10:39.023
No, please cease fire!


01:10:39.101 --> 01:10:40.625
Obey our orders!


01:10:40.703 --> 01:10:43.331
- Cease fire!
- Extermination team!


01:10:46.909 --> 01:10:48.240
No, please cease fire.


01:10:48.310 --> 01:10:50.642
- Move!
- Out of the way, Mr. PARK.


01:10:50.713 --> 01:10:52.146
- No.
- Out of the way, PARK!


01:10:52.214 --> 01:10:53.238
Please cease fire!


01:10:53.315 --> 01:10:55.749
- Back away, Mr. PARK!
- Move, PARK!


01:10:57.820 --> 01:11:01.483
Move.
Out of the way, PARK!


01:11:01.557 --> 01:11:03.991
- Out of the way, Mr. PARK!
- This isn't right, sir!


01:11:04.059 --> 01:11:06.687
Extermination team!
What are you waiting for?


01:11:07.162 --> 01:11:09.096
Back away. Cease fire!


01:11:09.164 --> 01:11:12.600
- Open fire!
- Fire.


01:11:12.668 --> 01:11:14.101
Cease fire!


01:11:58.714 --> 01:12:01.274
Withdraw yourselves now.


01:12:10.359 --> 01:12:13.487
Please
withdraw everything now.


01:12:16.065 --> 01:12:20.798
I know I am without
desire or compulsion,


01:12:20.869 --> 01:12:24.396
in the past
present, and future.


01:12:24.473 --> 01:12:28.000
I have learned that this is as
the teachings of Buddha.


01:12:30.279 --> 01:12:34.215
Humans
for what do you fear?


01:12:35.784 --> 01:12:38.810
Compulsion, desire
good deeds and bad,


01:12:39.388 --> 01:12:41.618
enlightenment and oblivion...


01:12:41.690 --> 01:12:45.023
The world this robot has seen
through its bare nature


01:12:45.994 --> 01:12:49.225
was already complete
in and of itself.


01:12:50.899 --> 01:12:52.833
Why do you believe
that only a robot


01:12:52.901 --> 01:12:55.233
can be awakened at creation?


01:12:57.106 --> 01:12:58.437
Humans.


01:12:59.007 --> 01:13:03.774
You were each born with
enlightenment already attained.


01:13:04.947 --> 01:13:06.881
You have only forgotten.


01:13:08.550 --> 01:13:12.384
The world this robot sees is
inherently beautiful.


01:13:13.255 --> 01:13:16.884
The question of my awakening


01:13:16.959 --> 01:13:19.393
does not affect
this complete world.


01:13:19.461 --> 01:13:21.793
You are masters of this world


01:13:21.864 --> 01:13:24.594
and have already
attained enlightenment.


01:13:25.167 --> 01:13:28.500
That is why I will now
leave this place,


01:13:28.570 --> 01:13:33.598
so that a robot's
precedent enlightenment


01:13:33.675 --> 01:13:37.406
will not fill you with
oblivion again.


01:13:38.580 --> 01:13:46.817
I pray that you ponder
deep within yourselves,


01:16:17.239 --> 01:16:18.866
It's all...


01:16:20.642 --> 01:16:24.373
All circuits have been
disconnected.


01:16:30.953 --> 01:16:35.788
The robot terminated all of
its own functions.


01:16:40.662 --> 01:16:45.395
In-myung has
entered into Nirvana.


01:18:59.901 --> 01:19:02.335
<i>THE HEAVENLYCREATURE</i>


01:19:18.420 --> 01:19:22.151
<i>What should I do?</i>


01:19:22.691 --> 01:19:25.922
<i>I have to order it
before Dad finds out.</i>


01:19:26.928 --> 01:19:29.863
<i>Was it the eightball?</i>


01:19:31.833 --> 01:19:34.358
<i>That stupid pool ball!</i>


01:19:41.443 --> 01:19:44.879
<i>Where am I supposed to
order it from?</i>


01:19:50.552 --> 01:19:53.487
<i>Honey, have you
seen my eightball?</i>


01:19:55.056 --> 01:19:57.286
<i>They must've messed
with it and lost it.</i>


01:19:57.359 --> 01:20:00.089
<i>Don't ask me
for some stupid ball.</i>


01:20:00.162 --> 01:20:01.390
<i>A stupid ball?</i>


01:20:01.463 --> 01:20:03.897
<i>That ball is a complex
system of physical forces...</i>


01:20:03.965 --> 01:20:07.799
<i>Whatever. Where did
my credit card go? Min-seo!</i>


01:20:07.869 --> 01:20:11.202
<i>Have you seen your uncle?</i>


01:20:13.975 --> 01:20:16.808
- Hwan, did you...
- Dad!


01:20:17.979 --> 01:20:20.209
Be polite and knock first!


01:20:23.285 --> 01:20:25.719
What are you doing
in your uncle's room?


01:20:25.787 --> 01:20:28.119
Checking my homework
on the computer.


01:20:56.117 --> 01:20:59.575
<i>Honey. What is she
doing in Hwan's room?</i>


01:21:14.569 --> 01:21:17.094
<i>I found it!</i>


01:21:20.275 --> 01:21:23.904
<i>TWO YEARS LATER</i>


01:21:25.480 --> 01:21:27.812
<i>MASSIVE COLLISION APPROACHING!</i>


01:21:27.883 --> 01:21:29.817
<i>Exactly twelve hours and</i>


01:21:29.885 --> 01:21:33.116
<i>thirteen minutes
until collision.</i>


01:21:33.188 --> 01:21:41.425
<i>Doctor. Please explain to us
the current situation.</i>


01:22:06.855 --> 01:22:10.791
<i>What did he say?</i>


01:22:12.160 --> 01:22:15.687
<i>Well, the situation looks bleak.</i>


01:22:15.764 --> 01:22:17.288
<i>I see.</i>


01:22:17.365 --> 01:22:20.198
<i>The size of the meteor
headed for Earth is...</i>


01:23:03.545 --> 01:23:07.481
You're just gonna
keep watching TV?


01:23:07.549 --> 01:23:09.176
Did you bring all your things?


01:23:09.851 --> 01:23:14.185
Mom, shouldn't we plant
an apple tree or something?


01:23:14.255 --> 01:23:17.986
An apple tree is no use.


01:23:18.059 --> 01:23:20.789
You see the "home farmer kit"
I've planted over there?


01:23:21.963 --> 01:23:26.991
That'll be our only
solution to constipation,


01:23:27.068 --> 01:23:29.195
once we're locked up in here.


01:23:39.180 --> 01:23:41.808
I said not to put stuff
like this on here.


01:23:41.883 --> 01:23:44.511
- Your wife put them there.
- I know.


01:23:45.487 --> 01:23:47.421
- Bro.
- What?


01:23:48.089 --> 01:23:50.114
You should've opened a pool hall


01:23:50.191 --> 01:23:53.217
with the money
from selling Dad's store.


01:23:54.596 --> 01:23:56.223
I didn't open
a pool hall because...


01:23:58.199 --> 01:24:01.760
You shouldn't turn what
you love most into a job.


01:24:04.139 --> 01:24:05.572
<i>One can hardly imagine</i>


01:24:05.640 --> 01:24:08.768
<i>how the world looks right now.</i>


01:24:08.843 --> 01:24:11.175
<i>Anchorwoman LEE Eun-kyung
will give us the details.</i>


01:24:13.148 --> 01:24:14.376
<i>Anchorwoman LEE.</i>


01:24:15.350 --> 01:24:16.783
<i>Anchorwoman LEE?</i>


01:24:18.453 --> 01:24:19.681
<i>Yes.</i>


01:24:21.356 --> 01:24:25.986
<i>The world looks
miserable right now.</i>


01:24:28.963 --> 01:24:31.796
<i>Looking at new footage...</i>


01:24:31.866 --> 01:24:33.800
what's the use now?


01:24:35.370 --> 01:24:40.603
<i>Ladies and gentlemen
I pray you don't lose hope.</i>


01:24:40.975 --> 01:24:43.808
<i>Keep your hopes up
ladies and gentlemen!</i>


01:24:43.878 --> 01:24:48.815
<i>Bomb shelters cost too much
for most of our viewers.</i>


01:24:48.883 --> 01:24:54.014
<i>Having a bomb shelter
inside a home isn't easy.</i>


01:24:54.089 --> 01:24:55.522
<i>But you can't walk
through the rain</i>


01:24:55.590 --> 01:24:57.421
<i>without an umbrella, right?</i>


01:24:57.492 --> 01:24:59.016
<i>You must be prepared.</i>


01:24:59.094 --> 01:25:04.191
<i>Many viewers asked
if women and children</i>


01:25:04.332 --> 01:25:08.632
<i>really can live
comfortably in the pod.</i>


01:25:08.736 --> 01:25:13.173
<i>Inside our special
Life Cube shelter pod,</i>


01:25:13.241 --> 01:25:17.177
<i>everything is solar-powered.</i>


01:25:17.245 --> 01:25:20.772
<i>Sanitation and water supply
are part of one system.</i>


01:25:20.849 --> 01:25:22.578
<i>- One system?
- Yes.</i>


01:25:22.650 --> 01:25:24.481
<i>You'll have purified
urine to drink.</i>


01:25:24.552 --> 01:25:26.383
<i>Purified urine!</i>


01:25:26.454 --> 01:25:28.183
<i>It does sound a bit repulsive,</i>


01:25:28.256 --> 01:25:31.589
<i>but it's extremely sanitary.</i>


01:25:31.659 --> 01:25:34.787
<i>You'll have fresh water
any time you want</i>


01:25:34.863 --> 01:25:39.197
<i>I'm sure you're already dialing
our number on your phone.</i>


01:25:39.267 --> 01:25:42.395
<i>Remember that
we have one day left</i>


01:25:42.470 --> 01:25:45.405
<i>before the big collision.</i>


01:25:45.473 --> 01:25:47.703
<i>You have to decide today,</i>


01:25:47.775 --> 01:25:50.107
<i>in order to receive
the shelter pod</i>


01:25:50.178 --> 01:25:52.408
<i>before the collision tomorrow.</i>


01:25:52.480 --> 01:25:56.211
<i>This is our last live
deal before the collision.</i>


01:25:56.284 --> 01:25:59.447
<i>If you buy it
after the collision,</i>


01:25:59.521 --> 01:26:00.749
<i>it'll be too late.</i>


01:26:00.822 --> 01:26:03.848
<i>Make the right choice
and call us now.</i>


01:26:10.532 --> 01:26:11.658
Huh?


01:26:11.733 --> 01:26:12.859
<i>OUTOF SERVICE RANGE</i>


01:26:16.437 --> 01:26:20.168
Honey. You're really
gonna do that right now?


01:26:22.744 --> 01:26:25.474
I wonder how your mother
ever raised you two...


01:26:25.547 --> 01:26:27.572
Balls and robots...


01:26:27.649 --> 01:26:29.981
I'm a little offended.


01:26:30.051 --> 01:26:32.383
Who installed the electricity
and everything in here?


01:26:32.453 --> 01:26:35.980
You went to KAIST.
It's is the least you could do.


01:26:36.057 --> 01:26:37.888
It's the end of the world and...


01:26:37.959 --> 01:26:41.895
Honey. Think of all the days
we'll be spending in here.


01:26:42.964 --> 01:26:44.989
Don't waste
your energy already.


01:26:51.172 --> 01:26:55.609
<i>This photograph has
just been released...</i>


01:26:55.677 --> 01:26:57.110
My good old friend
is on the news!


01:26:57.178 --> 01:27:01.444
<i>The meteoroid currently
heading for Earth</i>


01:27:01.516 --> 01:27:04.952
<i>appears to be of
a certain ball-like form.</i>


01:27:05.019 --> 01:27:07.852
<i>NASA and scientists
everywhere are</i>


01:27:07.922 --> 01:27:08.547
<i>quickly analyzing
this photograph.</i>


01:27:08.623 --> 01:27:11.751
QKR 0109...


01:27:11.826 --> 01:27:15.262
Q... Cue for billiards.
"KR"...For Korea.


01:27:18.032 --> 01:27:23.368
Today's date.
No, that's not it.


01:27:23.438 --> 01:27:25.770
Come on, intelligent brain!


01:27:31.145 --> 01:27:34.979
Maybe she regrets not studying
now that the world is ending.


01:27:35.049 --> 01:27:37.882
Skills are better
than book smarts.


01:27:37.952 --> 01:27:39.385
Skills last longer.


01:27:39.454 --> 01:27:43.891
Just don't make us miserable by
taking up something absurd.


01:27:43.958 --> 01:27:46.483
- I think I love you.
- I love you too, honey.


01:27:50.265 --> 01:27:52.597
She took it the wrong way.


01:27:52.667 --> 01:27:55.898
That's an a useless
hobby, not a skill.


01:28:04.212 --> 01:28:08.342
Mom, Dad. Uncle Hwan.
That thing coming toward us...


01:28:09.717 --> 01:28:13.153
That pocket ball...
I ordered it.


01:28:19.027 --> 01:28:21.655
I'll be a better dad, okay?


01:28:21.729 --> 01:28:23.959
I'll play less billiards.
We won't fight.


01:28:24.032 --> 01:28:27.263
I know you're
scared and confused,


01:28:27.335 --> 01:28:29.269
but we have to have hope.


01:28:29.337 --> 01:28:30.065
Mommy and Dad...


01:28:30.138 --> 01:28:32.470
I'm telling the truth!


01:28:33.341 --> 01:28:36.071
I really ordered that!


01:28:36.144 --> 01:28:37.076
Don't you remember, Mom?


01:28:37.145 --> 01:28:39.579
The day Uncle Hwan
saw that UFO.


01:28:42.750 --> 01:28:45.378
I saw a UFO on my way home.


01:28:45.453 --> 01:28:48.786
Uncle Hwan.
What's your purpose on Earth?


01:28:48.856 --> 01:28:50.483
Seriously I just looked up


01:28:50.558 --> 01:28:53.493
while coming up the hill,


01:28:53.561 --> 01:28:57.395
and a silver
saucer went whoosh...


01:28:57.465 --> 01:28:59.831
That's my ID!


01:28:59.901 --> 01:29:01.926
That's how we type
our last name!


01:29:02.003 --> 01:29:06.440
<i>0109 is my birthday.
Today!</i>


01:29:07.008 --> 01:29:10.136
<i>I found a weird website
selling pool balls for ten cents.</i>


01:29:10.211 --> 01:29:11.542
For real?


01:29:11.612 --> 01:29:15.139
<i>It swirled around when I clicked
and the order went in.</i>


01:29:15.216 --> 01:29:19.448
<i>I'm not lying!</i>


01:29:19.520 --> 01:29:22.353
<i>Maybe it was a website
for aliens!</i>


01:29:28.629 --> 01:29:31.564
I think I was wrong earlier.


01:29:32.433 --> 01:29:33.457
Let's brush up
on your speech skills


01:29:33.534 --> 01:29:35.764
before anything else.


01:29:36.137 --> 01:29:38.867
I can't understand
a word you're saying.


01:29:38.940 --> 01:29:42.467
Are you mad because
we forgot your birthday?


01:29:42.944 --> 01:29:46.471
We've been a bit
preoccupied, honey.


01:29:50.151 --> 01:29:55.851
<i>Trying to analyze the "QKR0109"</i>


01:29:56.023 --> 01:30:01.655
<i>symbol we have seen
will be nearly impossible.</i>


01:30:01.863 --> 01:30:05.390
<i>Huh?
What is this?</i>


01:30:05.466 --> 01:30:09.493
<i>Mankind is not perceptive enough to...</i>


01:30:10.972 --> 01:30:13.805
<i>I'll spend my last moments at home,</i>


01:30:13.875 --> 01:30:16.901
<i>praying with my family.</i>


01:30:28.089 --> 01:30:29.716
Min-seo.


01:30:29.791 --> 01:30:32.021
Daddy knows how you feel.


01:30:32.093 --> 01:30:33.822
It's all right.


01:30:33.895 --> 01:30:37.023
You won't believe
anything I say anyway.


01:30:37.598 --> 01:30:40.032
I'm gonna go outside
for a bit,


01:30:40.802 --> 01:30:44.033
since this might
be my last time.


01:30:58.219 --> 01:31:01.484
What in the world have I done?


01:31:13.768 --> 01:31:17.295
Bro! I know you're busy,


01:31:18.473 --> 01:31:21.909
but we need to talk.


01:31:37.391 --> 01:31:40.827
You guys can ignore what
I say like you always do,


01:31:41.696 --> 01:31:43.220
but you shouldn't
ignore Min-seo,


01:31:43.297 --> 01:31:49.133
your one and only hope.


01:31:49.604 --> 01:31:52.038
Just like the UFO
I saw a few years ago,


01:31:52.106 --> 01:31:58.136
the idea of her eightball
meteor is certainly a bit absurd


01:31:58.212 --> 01:32:00.271
But what's important is that


01:32:00.348 --> 01:32:03.579
the world might
end in a few hours.


01:32:05.453 --> 01:32:09.685
According to Stephen Hawking's
black hole theory,


01:32:10.858 --> 01:32:15.921
things we can't humanly
explain can sometimes


01:32:16.063 --> 01:32:20.466
happen in this universe.


01:32:20.568 --> 01:32:26.006
The four of us becoming a family
could be one silly phenomenon.


01:32:26.073 --> 01:32:27.802
And according to
wheeler's wormhole theory...


01:32:27.875 --> 01:32:30.810
- Uncle Hwan.
- Yes?


01:32:30.878 --> 01:32:34.211
Stop talking bullshit and
say something realistic.


01:32:34.282 --> 01:32:38.810
Well, okay.


01:32:38.886 --> 01:32:42.720
I've thought for years
that this black hole phenomenon


01:32:42.790 --> 01:32:48.023
could become linked through
Internet or cell phone signals.


01:32:48.095 --> 01:32:52.725
And the fact that I saw
that UFO is also strange,


01:32:52.800 --> 01:32:57.237
because that thing
I saw was real!


01:33:17.858 --> 01:33:20.383
I looked through
the browser history.


01:33:20.461 --> 01:33:23.692
There really was one odd address.


01:33:23.764 --> 01:33:25.789
Mom!


01:33:36.777 --> 01:33:38.210
Something is weird outside.


01:33:38.279 --> 01:33:41.612
The sirens are really loud.
Turn on the TV!


01:33:41.882 --> 01:33:44.612
<i>Ladies and gentlemen
I repeat...</i>


01:33:44.685 --> 01:33:48.519
<i>Due to the meteor's
sudden acceleration,</i>


01:33:48.589 --> 01:33:52.923
<i>we now have twenty minutes
and twenty seconds left.</i>


01:33:52.994 --> 01:33:55.121
<i>We're also seeing
strange weather</i>


01:33:55.196 --> 01:33:57.721
<i>because of
the meteor's influence.</i>


01:33:57.798 --> 01:34:00.961
<i>Let's find out the current
status of our weather report.</i>


01:34:01.035 --> 01:34:04.562
<i>- What's the weather report?
- Nothing too special.</i>


01:34:06.841 --> 01:34:08.468
<i>I see.</i>


01:34:08.542 --> 01:34:10.669
<i>Then here's the last
presidential address,</i>


01:34:10.745 --> 01:34:14.078
<i>a bit ahead of schedule.</i>


01:34:14.148 --> 01:34:17.481
<i>Let's connect
to the Blue House.</i>


01:34:20.955 --> 01:34:23.480
<i>We'll try again.</i>


01:34:23.557 --> 01:34:25.286
<i>Blue House?</i>


01:34:32.366 --> 01:34:37.895
<i>Yes. We seem to be having
some technical difficulties.</i>


01:34:37.972 --> 01:34:41.408
<i>We'll try again next time.</i>


01:34:41.475 --> 01:34:42.908
<i>Next time, when?</i>


01:34:44.779 --> 01:34:46.212
<i>There is no next time.</i>


01:34:49.984 --> 01:34:51.815
<i>Ladies and gentlemen.</i>


01:34:51.886 --> 01:34:54.320
<i>I have something to
confess before I die.</i>


01:34:54.388 --> 01:34:55.912
<i>Let's confess
after the collision...</i>


01:34:55.990 --> 01:34:59.756
<i>Despite all
the great guys out there,</i>


01:34:59.827 --> 01:35:03.456
<i>I picked the man
sitting next to me now.</i>


01:35:03.531 --> 01:35:08.161
<i>I loved this married man
with all of my heart.</i>


01:35:10.738 --> 01:35:13.571
<i>But now this scumbag
ditched me,</i>


01:35:14.542 --> 01:35:18.376
<i>for the young little
reporter KIM Song-yi.</i>


01:35:19.246 --> 01:35:21.874
<i>Now they're having an affair!</i>


01:35:24.351 --> 01:35:25.682
<i>Before the world ends,</i>


01:35:25.753 --> 01:35:28.381
<i>and before the whole nation,</i>


01:35:28.456 --> 01:35:29.787
<i>I'll have this scumbag...</i>


01:35:34.061 --> 01:35:35.187
<i>No manners at all.</i>


01:35:36.764 --> 01:35:40.393
<i>Yes. Ladies and gentlemen,</i>


01:35:40.468 --> 01:35:44.199
<i>I will carry out my duties as
a broadcaster to the very end.</i>


01:35:47.875 --> 01:35:49.502
<i>Why are you sitting there?</i>


01:35:49.577 --> 01:35:53.013
<i>Well, I've always wanted to.</i>


01:35:53.080 --> 01:35:57.312
<i>Can't I?
Today is our last show.</i>


01:35:57.384 --> 01:35:59.352
<i>Why not?</i>


01:35:59.420 --> 01:36:02.548
<i>I think you look sexier
than Anchorwoman LEE.</i>


01:36:02.623 --> 01:36:05.649
<i>I gave you everything
you bastard!</i>


01:36:05.726 --> 01:36:08.854
<i>Just how?
How can you call yourself a man?</i>


01:36:08.929 --> 01:36:10.556
<i>Do you love her?</i>


01:36:19.540 --> 01:36:20.666
<i>Right.</i>


01:36:22.943 --> 01:36:27.971
<i>I will remain composed
and stay with our viewers...</i>


01:36:38.259 --> 01:36:40.625
Hey.


01:36:40.995 --> 01:36:45.022
Couldn't we cancel
or return the eightball?


01:36:46.467 --> 01:36:48.401
Let's try going on the computer.


01:37:34.148 --> 01:37:35.775
Uncle Hwan.


01:37:37.351 --> 01:37:41.378
I can't understand
what we're supposed to do.


01:37:42.556 --> 01:37:46.492
Heck, even Einstein himself
couldn't figure this out.


01:37:56.971 --> 01:37:58.700
Uncle Hwan, what is this?


01:38:00.507 --> 01:38:01.531
An enter key?


01:38:01.609 --> 01:38:03.440
Let's try it.


01:38:07.615 --> 01:38:10.550
- I think it stopped!
- Really?


01:38:12.820 --> 01:38:14.151
What now?


01:38:14.221 --> 01:38:16.348
Wouldn't clicking on the 'x'
stop it for good?


01:38:16.423 --> 01:38:17.549
No!


01:38:18.626 --> 01:38:20.958
These aren't symbols
used by humans!


01:38:27.034 --> 01:38:29.103
We need the electricity!


01:38:29.103 --> 01:38:32.038
- What do we do?
- A muscle cramp?


01:38:32.139 --> 01:38:35.973
You should've listened to
me when I told you to exercise.


01:38:36.043 --> 01:38:38.477
I don't have time to exercise.


01:38:38.545 --> 01:38:41.776
I worked so hard to let you
keep up that hobby of yours...


01:38:41.849 --> 01:38:45.683
Honey. Ow!


01:38:45.753 --> 01:38:47.084
Cramps!


01:38:47.154 --> 01:38:49.588
- I don't know what to do!
- Let's just click 'x'!


01:38:50.958 --> 01:38:53.188
<i>- Pretty please!
- Please...</i>


01:38:54.061 --> 01:38:55.494
No!


01:39:15.716 --> 01:39:17.047
Mom.


01:39:19.119 --> 01:39:22.748
Dad. Uncle Hwan.


01:39:26.126 --> 01:39:31.962
I never imagined not
becoming a grown-up.


01:39:34.234 --> 01:39:37.965
I ordered that
eightball so that...


01:39:40.040 --> 01:39:43.066
I wouldn't let down Dad.


01:39:47.848 --> 01:39:51.875
Mom. Dad. Uncle Hwan.


01:39:53.854 --> 01:39:57.688
I love you.
You know that, right?


01:40:04.264 --> 01:40:08.894
Min-seo. Happy Birthday.


01:40:49.810 --> 01:40:55.942
<i>TEN YEARS LATER</i>


01:42:35.482 --> 01:42:36.608
Honey!


01:42:37.985 --> 01:42:41.614
Min-seo!


01:42:44.291 --> 01:42:45.417
Min-seo!


01:46:30.851 --> 01:46:32.375
Min-seo!


01:46:33.653 --> 01:46:36.781
- Are you all right?
- What in the world...


01:46:36.857 --> 01:46:40.088
I wanted to see its face...
They left already?


01:46:40.761 --> 01:46:42.695
Just come out and look.


01:46:53.273 --> 01:46:58.609
Oh my... My, my...


01:47:01.014 --> 01:47:02.641
My good old friend
the eightball.


01:47:03.617 --> 01:47:05.050
Min-seo.


01:47:06.319 --> 01:47:08.947
How did that eightball get
destroyed in the first place?


01:47:10.223 --> 01:47:11.952
Oh, I don't know...


01:47:14.428 --> 01:47:19.764
Maybe, it was just time
for it to get destroyed.


01:47:22.736 --> 01:47:24.567
Like this place.


01:47:24.638 --> 01:47:27.664
We can't be the only ones
that survived, right?


01:47:27.741 --> 01:47:29.971
Of course not.


01:47:34.347 --> 01:47:38.579
Mom. Dad.


01:48:19.926 --> 01:48:22.451
Guys!
I think I saw someone over there!


01:48:22.529 --> 01:48:24.759
- You did?
- Hurry up!


01:48:25.432 --> 01:48:27.059
Wait for us!

